  "94847356-dafd-4936-8df4-52a170ba64ac": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p4-information",
     "replacement": "A **fractional index** $\\frac{1}{n}$ means the $n$th root. The denominator is the index of the surd, where $n$ is an integer with $n\\geq2$. For even $n$, $a\\geq0$. For odd $n$, $a$ can be any real number.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}a^{\\frac{1}{2}}&=\\sqrt{a}\\\\a^{\\frac{1}{3}}&=\\sqrt[3]{a}\\\\a^{\\frac{1}{n}}&=\\sqrt[n]{a}\\end{aligned}$$",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p4-information",
     "targetFingerprint": "915534f954308e1235b8c4a4c3f054c3fe717f34343ff112f54cebb01874bdb6",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/fractional-indices-v1/20261109-224221",
   "revision": 40
  },
  "47e1b8ad-8876-4d80-9a02-a0df6ca4d744": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p10-information-block",
     "replacement": "- The **denominator** $n$ is the index of the surd.\n- The **numerator** $m$ is the power.\n\n$$a^{\\frac{m}{n}}=\\sqrt[n]{a^m}=\\left(\\sqrt[n]{a}\\right)^m$$\nHere $m$ and $n$ are integers with $n\\geq2$, and $a\\geq0$ when $n$ is even. A negative index gives the reciprocal: $a^{-\\frac{m}{n}}=\\dfrac{1}{a^{\\frac{m}{n}}}$, for $a\\ne0$.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p10-information-block",
     "targetFingerprint": "9c7fd023cba09df06746daccd3bd1fdc2b5fc9bd930f97a33b7f49c48e75370e",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/fractional-indices-v1/20261109-224221",
   "revision": 40
  },
  "47791d03-2fff-4728-838b-31a681c0c405": {
   "kind": "theory-wording",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p14-key-ideas-block",
     "replacement": "- Surds can be written with fractional indices, so all the index laws apply to surds.\n- To change an expression from index form to surd form, deal with negative indices first.",
